        "thinking": "So `undici@7.24.4` is pulled in by `better-auth` → `vitest` (as a peer) → `jsdom`. The server package also has `jsdom` as a direct dependency.\n\nBut `vitest` is normally a devDependency, and `jsdom` is vitest's peer. It shouldn't be bundled in a production worker build. However, when the server package is imported, esbuild may traverse ALL dependencies, not just the ones actually imported.\n\nActually wait - in pnpm, the packages are available at `node_modules/.pnpm/...` and symlinked. \n\nThe key question is whether `better-auth` actually imports `undici` at runtime or if it's just a transitive peer dependency through vitest and jsdom. If `better-auth` doesn't directly depend on `undici`, esbuild shouldn't bundle it unless the server package itself pulls in jsdom. So the server package itself has `jsdom` listed as a direct production dependency, which is why `undici@7` is being pulled in—it's a transitive dependency of jsdom. I need to check the server's package.json to confirm jsdom is actually declared there as a production dependency rather than a dev dependency.",
